---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="Read how Kreativ Auto approaches research, recommendations, and publishing standards.">
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface p-8 sm:p-10">
      <p class="eyebrow">Editorial Policy</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">How content is approached</h1>
      <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-base leading-7 text-steel">
        <p>Kreativ Auto is written with a bias toward clarity, usefulness, and practical judgment.</p>
        <p>Problem guides are meant to help readers narrow down likely causes before spending money blindly. Best-parts pages are meant to compare reasonable options, not pad out a list for the sake of having more links.</p>
        <p>Recommendations are based on fitment relevance, reputation, expected use case, and overall practicality for normal drivers.</p>
        <p>Automotive content should never replace proper inspection, service information, or professional diagnosis when safety is involved. The site is here to help readers ask better questions and make better decisions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
